&lt;h1 id=&#34;voice-conversion-based-anonymization&#34;&gt;Voice conversion based anonymization&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;voice-conversion&#34;&gt;Voice conversion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logical speaker anonymization framework
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert &lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;source&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt; speaker&amp;rsquo;s voice to a &lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;target&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt; speaker&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversion may not be perfect, residual &lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;source&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt; speaker info might be present&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Choice of &lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;target&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt; speaker is critical for strength of anonymization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allows data publication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First proposed in 2009 [2], many techniques proposed thereafter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;vc-methods-criteria&#34;&gt;VC methods: criteria&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-parallel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Many-to-many&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source/language independent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;three-vc-methods&#34;&gt;Three VC methods&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;VoiceMask&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;: simple frequency warping based on composition of two functions $B$ and $Q$: $ f&amp;rsquo; = B(Q(f, \alpha), \beta) $&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;Vocal Tract Length Normalization&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;: learn transformation parameters between source and target class spectra&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;Disentangled Speech Representation&lt;!-- raw HTML omitted --&gt;: separate encoders for &lt;strong&gt;content&lt;/strong&gt; (instance normalization) and &lt;strong&gt;speaker&lt;/strong&gt; (average pooling) information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
